A||||4||Eric||Heads.  Why won't these work?
Z||000000||Eric||07-08-99||05:03 PM||||Why won't the aluminum heads work on our 2.8s?  I was just at a local machine shop, where they have done head work for the past 300 years, and the owner told me the aluminum 3.1 heads would work perfectly on my 2.8.  Then, as said previously by some of you guys, I told him the intake manifold wouldn't match up.  He basically told me I was full of crap and he would know what matches and what don't because he has been doing this for the past 300 years.  <p>My question now is, can the intake be ported to match the head or is it hopeless?  If I can't get new aluminum heads, what kind of work should I get done to the iron ones (the 3.1 heads had a three angle valve job but no porting or polishing)?  I will get the heads done at this guy's shop even though he may have steered me in the wrong direction, just because he seems to know his stuff about everthing else, but I guess anybody would after 300 years in the business.
Z||000001||PaUL||07-08-99||05:08 PM||||Yes the alum. heads wont fit the stock fiero intake manifold. The port spacing is completely different, no amount of machining will make them match up. 
Z||000002||batboy||07-08-99||06:00 PM||||I believe the aluminum heads will bolt up to the block, but you have to use an intake manifold that fits those heads. I wonder if there is any aftermarket carb manifold for the aluminum "Generation II" heads. Also, the pistons are different on these engines, because the heads are a higher compression ratio and the valves are splayed in different positions.
Z||000003||GREENDANO||07-08-99||06:04 PM||||Tell the dinosaur that the heads WILL bolt up yes.  But Gen II 2.8/3.1 aluminum heads have equal intake spacing while the iron heads are asymetrical port spacing.  It's more than just a mater of "gasket matching" the ports, it's a matter of redesigning the motor/manifolds.  Plus, the aluminum heads need the correct "pop-up" pistons that match or you'll have really low compression.<br>  Dan-O
Z||000004||Hock||07-09-99||11:29 AM||||I bought one of those engines for my Fiero and to tell you the true so far it was a waste of money. I have to get different heads, an aftermarket intake, and everything else to make it work. <br>Yes, the heads will bolt up to the block BUT your factory intake will not bolt up to those heads. Yes, they are lighter, have a smaller combustion camber, but they just work work unless you get that style intake with them.<br>Finnaly, you do not need pop up pistons on that engine because the heads have such small combustion cambers flattop pistons would be enough to get the compression up to 9.5-10:1. <br>SO, there you go, the 300 year old man obiviusly has no clue what he is talking about in this case.
